{
  "reasons": {
    "other-verse-lev-1-8": "LXX2012's English of this verse renders the Greek of the neighbouring verse, so the Greek words that render it are in that verse and have no chunk here to point at (Leviticus 1:1's 'Speak to the children of Israel' is Swete's 1:2 Λάλησον τοῖς υἱοῖς Ἰσραήλ; 1:11's 'lay his hand on its head' is Swete's 1:10; 2:9's 'approach the altar' Swete's 2:8; the English under Swete's 6:4 also renders Swete's 6:5, and that under 8:18 also 8:19; the English under 8:20 ends with the washing that opens Swete's 8:21, and that under 8:22 with the killing that opens 8:23): the like of Genesis 37:32 (mw-u2w5klk.349.9, mw-u2w5klk.349.134).",
    "added-clause-lev-1-8": "Brenton prints the list of Leviticus 8:30 twice, once for the sprinkling and again after a clause 'And he sanctified Aaron'; Swete's 8:30 has the list once and no sanctifying clause, so the second printing has no Greek word to point at (mw-u2w5klk.349.134).",
    "paired-or-added-lev-1-8": "Either the Greek word that renders it is a pair the aligner made to another English word of its phrase that no fix row has yet moved (the 'offering' and 'whole' of 'whole burnt offering' beside ὁλοκαύτωμα, the 'flour' of 'fine flour' beside σεμίδαλις, 'take away', 'pour out' and 'brought near' beside one Greek verb), or Brenton's English adds it to turn a Greek phrase into English ('forth', 'thing', 'things', 'matter', 'seven' of 'seven times'); each was read against its verse (mw-u2w5klk.349.9)."
  },
